<div id="life">
<h2>Life</h2>

<img src="mahatma_gandhi.jpg">
<p> Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi was the leader of India's non-violent independence movement against British rule and a world-renowned advocate for civil rights. </p>
</div>

<div id="works">
<h2>Works</h2>
<p><b>Satyagraha</b> - He pioneered the philosophy of non-violent resistance, leading famous movements like the Dandi Salt March to protest unfair British taxes.</p>
<p><b>Social Reform</b> - He worked tirelessly to abolish the practice of untouchability and promoted communal harmony between different religious groups.</p>
<p><b>Swadeshi Movement</b> - He encouraged Indians to boycott foreign goods and spin their own cloth (Khadi) to achieve economic self-reliance.</p>
</div>

<div id="legacy">
<h2>Legacy</h2>
<p>Gandhi's legacy of "Ahimsa" (non-violence) and "Truth" inspired leaders worldwide, including Martin Luther King Jr. and Nelson Mandela, in their fight for justice.</p>
</div>

